{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792445890,"nonce":"ALGhh7XC1hXaXby26SZB/Ozd070=","message":"Separate document data from mounted CodeEditor views\n\nCodeEditorState now owns the shared text signal, bounded CodeHistory, cached CodeDocument/annotations, and saved selection/scroll. CodeEditor accepts state instead of value, captures navigation on unmount, and releases its view capture hook. A generation token handles keyed replacement mounting before the old view is disposed.\n\nAn inactive state contains no TextEditing, CodeMetrics, row/token pools, Canvas/minimap or reactive owner. External source replacement while unmounted clears incompatible history on remount. Dropping the state releases document/history caches.\n\nValidation: CodeStateLifecycle passes 20 checks across dark/light, including unmount/ref/host removal, model identity, selection/folds/scroll restoration, undo/redo, replacement ordering and external text reset. Existing CodeComponents passes all 266 checks. RayDE's document lifecycle snapshots pass in both themes, including closed clean cache eviction and closed unsaved text/history retained until saved.","files":null}]}